ENV-GHG-003F	Scope 3 – Waste Generated in Operations	Indirect GHG emissions from the disposal and treatment of solid and liquid waste generated at MEIL's construction sites and facilities: C&D debris (landfill / recycled), municipal solid waste from site camps and offices, hazardous waste (oily rags, spent solvents, contaminated soil), e-waste (cables, switchgear), and wastewater. Calculate using waste quantity (tonnes) × disposal route emission factor (tCO2e/t). Factors from CPCB SWM Report 2022–23, MoEFCC C&D Waste Management Rules 2016, IPCC 2006 Waste Chapter (India Tier 1 methane correction factors).	environment	Section C	6	essential	t	Scope 3 GHG – Waste in Operations	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	maker	CALC-GHG-SCOPE3-WASTE	9992f9db-5a5a-46f2-ac25-db784537d5d9	2026-10-06 12:45:06.932344+00	2026-10-06 16:57:30.510034+00	f	project	Enter total waste generated at site by category: C&D debris (MT), MSW from camp (MT), hazardous waste (MT), and disposal route (landfill/recycled/treated).	GHG Protocol Category 5 (Waste in Operations). Mandated under SEBI BRSR Principle 6 E7 and C&D Waste Management Rules 2016.	Upload waste manifest from authorized recycler/disposal facility, or site waste register signed by EHS officer.
ENV-GHG-003D	Scope 3 – Upstream Transportation and Logistics	Indirect GHG emissions from transportation of purchased goods and materials to MEIL's facilities in vehicles not owned or controlled by MEIL: third-party logistics trucks, rail freight. Use tonne-km × freight emission factor (HCV diesel / Indian Railways). Source: CPCB / MoPNG / Indian Railways 2022–23.	environment	Section C	6	leadership	f	\N	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	conditional	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE3-LOGISTICS	a24ae4da-5f8d-4f08-94a3-84fe3dfbc722	2026-10-06 12:45:06.932333+00	2026-10-06 16:57:30.510035+00	f	project	Enter total tonne-kilometres of material transported to this site by third-party logistics (road trucks, rail freight) during the month.	GHG Protocol Category 4 (Upstream Transport). Logistics is coordinated at project level where goods receipt happens.	Upload goods receipt note (GRN) with transport distance, or third-party logistics provider monthly invoice showing tonne-km.
ENV-ENERGY-002	Fuel consumption (diesel, petrol, gas)	Capture fuel consumption in physical units (litres, kL, kg) converted to gigajoules (GJ) using documented calorific factors.	environment	Section C	6	essential	f	\N	numeric	GJ	["Litres", "kL", "GJ"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	\N	c14ed3cd-7197-40ff-8cd1-edb6d5b52221	2026-10-06 12:45:06.932203+00	2026-10-06 16:57:30.510037+00	f	project	Enter total fuel consumed (diesel, petrol, LPG, natural gas) in physical units. Do not convert — the system calculates GJ automatically.	Required for Scope 1 GHG calculation under SEBI BRSR Principle 6 and BEE PAT scheme reporting.	Upload fuel delivery challan from IOCL/BPCL/HPCL, or DG logbook stamped by site engineer.
ENV-GHG-003A	Scope 3 – Business Travel	Indirect GHG emissions from employee travel on business in vehicles not owned or controlled by MEIL: domestic and international flights, Indian Railways (trains), road travel by hired taxi/cab. Calculate using distance (passenger-km) × mode emission factor. Source: Indian Railways Sustainability Report / DGCA / MoPNG / IPCC 2006.	environment	Section C	6	essential	t	Scope 3 GHG – Business Travel	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE3-TRAVEL	dc8ebc69-d0ae-41fc-ae01-0f44c22c58f5	2026-10-06 12:45:06.932316+00	2026-10-06 16:57:30.934483+00	f	business_unit	Enter total business travel by air, rail, and road for all employees of this BU during the month. Enter passenger-kilometres per travel mode.	GHG Protocol Category 6 (Business Travel). Mandated under SEBI BRSR Core for Scope 3 disclosure. HR/Finance is the source of truth for travel data.	Upload monthly travel expense report from HR system, or consolidated airline/rail booking statement from travel desk (Yatra, MakeMyTrip corporate).
ENV-GHG-003B	Scope 3 – Employee Commuting	Indirect GHG emissions from employee commuting between home and workplace in vehicles not owned by MEIL: site buses hired, personal vehicles, public transport. Use distance (km/day × working days) × occupancy × emission factor. Source: MoPNG PPAC / IPCC 2006.	environment	Section C	6	essential	f	\N	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	conditional	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE3-COMMUTE	e28ee6e9-9428-4447-b2d9-1157ce2af2ae	2026-10-06 12:45:06.932323+00	2026-10-06 16:57:30.93449+00	f	business_unit	Enter total employee commuting distance per mode (private car, hired bus, public transport) for all BU staff during the month.	GHG Protocol Category 7 (Employee Commuting). Captured at BU level using HR headcount and average commute distance surveys.	Upload HR commute survey summary report or employee transport vendor records (bus contractor monthly bill).
ENV-GHG-001B-DSL	Scope 1 – Mobile Combustion (Diesel / HSD)	Direct GHG emissions from mobile combustion in diesel-powered vehicles and construction equipment: excavators, dump trucks, cranes, compactors, and transit mixers. Calculated as Litres × 0.00268 tCO2e/L. Source: BEE PAT Manual 2023 / MoPNG PPAC.	environment	Section C	6	essential	t	Scope 1 GHG – Mobile Diesel	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE1-MOBILE-DIESEL	f62fe998-3878-49e6-bcb2-a59db72923a6	2026-10-06 20:20:18.161419+00	2026-10-06 20:20:18.16143+00	f	project	Enter diesel/HSD fuel consumed in mobile construction equipment and transport vehicles.	Scope 1 mobile diesel combustion under SEBI BRSR Principle 6 Indicator E1.	Upload vehicle diesel logbook or HSD fuel dispenser meter readings.
ENV-GHG-001B-PET	Scope 1 – Mobile Combustion (Petrol / MS)	Direct GHG emissions from petrol-fueled fleet vehicles, site inspection cars, and light commercial vehicles. Calculated as Litres × 0.00231 tCO2e/L. Source: BEE PAT Manual 2023 / MoPNG PPAC.	environment	Section C	6	essential	t	Scope 1 GHG – Mobile Petrol	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE1-MOBILE-PETROL	7b90e2f1-75c1-4dd5-84fa-4217c669d189	2026-10-06 20:20:18.161462+00	2026-10-06 20:20:18.161465+00	f	project	Enter petrol consumed in company-owned/leased cars and utility vehicles.	Scope 1 mobile petrol combustion under SEBI BRSR Principle 6 Indicator E1.	Upload petrol pump fuel slips or fleet card monthly summary.
ENV-GHG-001B-CNG	Scope 1 – Mobile Combustion (CNG)	Direct GHG emissions from Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) powered buses, vans, and light commercial vehicles. Calculated as kg × 0.00221 tCO2e/kg. Source: MoPNG PPAC 2023 / MoEFCC.	environment	Section C	6	essential	t	Scope 1 GHG – Mobile CNG	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE1-MOBILE-CNG	fbca30bd-1192-4885-896b-59e7ecabd048	2026-10-06 20:20:18.161487+00	2026-10-06 20:20:18.16149+00	f	project	Enter CNG quantity consumed in company fleet vehicles in kg.	Scope 1 mobile CNG combustion under SEBI BRSR Principle 6 Indicator E1.	Upload CNG filling station receipts or fleet logbook.
ENV-GHG-001D-REF	Scope 1 – Fugitive Emissions (Refrigerant Leaks)	Direct fugitive GHG emissions from HVAC and AC refrigerant leakage and top-ups (HCFC-22, HFC-32, HFC-410A). Calculated as top-up quantity (kg) × AR4 100-yr GWP. Source: IPCC AR4 / MoEFCC India.	environment	Section C	6	essential	f	\N	numeric	tCO2e	["tCO2e", "kgCO2e"]	sum	\N	\N	mandatory	monthly	site_collector	CALC-GHG-SCOPE1-FUGITIVE-REFRIGERANT	a3455918-9d06-4a36-9f78-5e8b8759e9a9	2026-10-06 20:20:18.16151+00	2026-10-06 20:20:18.161513+00	f	project	Enter refrigerant gas quantity refilled in HVAC and cooling systems in kg.	Scope 1 fugitive refrigerant emissions under SEBI BRSR Principle 6.	Upload HVAC maintenance service log or refrigerant gas purchase invoice.
